Possibly permissions (maybe try as Administrator?), possibly anti-virus (disable internet and turn-off AV?), possibly conflicting with a previous installation of Cygwin stuff (uninstall old or try rebaseall), possibly trying to access uninitialized memory (I just pushed a change to make/win that unsurpressed some uninitialized warnings on Windows), or possibly something else. But most likely we will be able to fix it somehow.

Ben

