I think we're in agreement: a cov_matrix defaults to a Cholesky factor parameterization, and other forms can be explicitly instantiated by the user.

The CovMatrix class would allow Stan to be smarter about how covariance matrices are used when computing likelihoods.

So in summary, this is proposing to add a chol_factor and corr_matrix type to the modeling language.  Beyond that maybe also a way to specify a vector of positive reals?  The CovMatrix class can be added somewhat independently of this.

Cheers,
Marcus

