I think it shouldn't make much of a difference; either using an
explicit constant or adding a column of 1s in the design matrix should
be about the same. I tried using an explicit intercept term instead of
a column of ones in a 24-dimensional (plus intercept) logistic
regression:

y[i] ~ bernoulli_logit(alpha + dot_product(beta, x_without_one[i]))

and the result was maybe around 5% slower (there's a nontrivial
uncertainty interval around that number). So I wouldn't sweat it too
much.

