Not that we shouldn't have a templated version or else versions for each thing separately, but stan often uses a std::vector, an Eigen::vector, or an Eigen::Array interchangeably and arbitrarily. And we haven't gotten around to standardizing on matrix_v, vector_v, etc. So, whenever that happens we should probably standardize on some conventions for when to use std::vector, an Eigen::vector, or an Eigen::Array. Personally, I would say that a function be defined on an Eigen::vector or an Eigen::matrix iff the function is doing matrix algebra such as dot products.

Also, it would be good if there were an optimized implementation for the dot product of a vector with itself.

Ben

