As a first cut, we can use the .eval() postfix to evaluate an expression immediately. If I am understanding correctly, adding all the .eval() postfixes would essentially yield the same performance that we have now but would allow us to eliminate or simplify code. We could then gradually remove the .eval() postfixes and replace them with our own templated versions where there are performance bottlenecks.

