It's not quite true that we use the expression templates right now.  Any time we write multiply() or add() or dot_product() in the code, the expression gets evaluated to an Eigen::Matrix, i.e., .eval() is already implicitly called all over the place.  Since those functions are the only sensible way to write templated functions like multi_normal_log, they are the primary ones that get used.

