> Couldn't a bunch of cases could be covered by
>
> return c * y_true + (!c) * y_false;
>
> particularly if you define multiplication between a bool and a var appropriately.

It may be better to not template on the first argument, like

     template <typename T>
     T if_else(bool c, T y_true, T y_false) {

       return c * y_true + (!c) * y_false;
     }

because the C++'11 standard codifies conversion of anything to bool in the de facto way of testing whether c != 0.

Ben

